.TH "EPX\-ORDERS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-orders \- read, create and change orders and their status
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders [flags]
epx orders [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads, creates and changes sales orders, personal data included, and their status: \fBepx orders transition\fR moves an order to another status, \fBadd\-entries\fR and \fBrecalculate\fR change its entries, and \fBsplit\fR splits it into sub\-orders by vendor.
.PP
Its reads require the order.order_read scope. Its writes require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx orders add\-entries"
Add products to an order, or change its entries.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders add\-entries ORDER_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Adds products to the order ORDER_ID, or changes the quantity of its entries, and recalculates it: the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR holds entries, each with the productId of a product to add or the entryId of an entry to change (an id in the order\(aqs entries, as \fBepx orders get ID \-o json\fR prints them), and its quantity; 0 removes the entry. Emporix answers with the order recalculated, which it stores only with \fB\-\-store\fR: without it, the order stays as it is. Emporix refuses to change the entries of a COMPLETED order with 400 Bad Request (exit 1).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the order.order_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-store\fR
Store the recalculated order; without it, Emporix only answers with it.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx orders count"
Count orders.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders count [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Prints the number of sales orders, or of those that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR), which Emporix reports in a header without sending the orders: a master order and each of its sub\-orders count once, as list lists them. \fB\-o json\fR prints the number alone. Emporix counts 0 for a filter on id or customer.id although list finds the orders (seen live): list them instead.
.PP
Requires the order.order_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among COUNT.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.SS "epx orders create"
Create an order.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates an order on behalf of a customer from the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR, shaped as \fBepx orders get ID \-o json\fR prints one (entries, customer, siteCode, currency and calculatedPrice among others). Emporix makes the order\(aqs id and answers with it: an id in the body is ignored, so sending the body again creates another order (with checkout true, at most one per cartId). It stores the status CREATED for IN_CHECKOUT, and sets mixins.generalAttributes (extendedOrderStatus \fB"10"\fR, orderNumber and customerFirstOrder) whatever the body says; \fBepx orders patch\fR can change them afterwards, e.g. to make the order ready for \fBepx invoice\-jobs create\fR. It also adds an address of the order to the customer\(aqs addresses, as a default one tagged shipping and billing, so a customer who had a default address then has two default addresses.
.PP
Give the order\(aqs and its entries\(aq metadata.mixins the URLs of the schemas of their mixins, as orders placed in a checkout carry them: without them, \fBepx orders add\-entries \-\-store\fR, \fBrecalculate\fR, \fBpatch \-\-recalculate\fR and \fBsplit\fR fail on the order with 400 Bad Request (exit 1).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the order.order_create scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx orders delete"
Delete one order.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the order ID; it sends no body. ID is the ID that \fBepx orders list\fR shows.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the order.order_delete scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx orders get"
Show one order.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads sales orders, personal data included. TYPE is MASTER_ORDER or SUB_ORDER for an order split, for example by vendor: the master and its sub\-orders are all listed, so do not add up their totals. STATUS is IN_CHECKOUT, CREATED, CONFIRMED, DECLINED, SHIPPED or COMPLETED, CUSTOMER the customer\(aqs email (or name), ITEMS the number of order entries and TOTAL the gross final price in the order\(aqs currency (empty when Emporix sends only the deprecated totalPrice, which \fB\-o json\fR shows, as for an order that \fBepx orders add\-entries \-\-store\fR, \fBrecalculate\fR or \fBsplit\fR rewrote, and for sub\-orders). The orders of a legal entity: \fBepx orders list \-\-query legalEntityId:ID\fR.
.PP
Requires the order.order_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, STATUS, CREATED, CUSTOMER, SITE, ITEMS, TOTAL.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx orders history"
Show the status changes of an order.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders history ORDER_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the status changes of an order, in the order Emporix sends them. \fB\-o json\fR adds the history\(aqs metadata. ORDER_ID is the ID that \fBepx orders list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
Requires the order.order_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among STATUS, TIMESTAMP.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx orders list"
List orders.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads sales orders, personal data included. TYPE is MASTER_ORDER or SUB_ORDER for an order split, for example by vendor: the master and its sub\-orders are all listed, so do not add up their totals. STATUS is IN_CHECKOUT, CREATED, CONFIRMED, DECLINED, SHIPPED or COMPLETED, CUSTOMER the customer\(aqs email (or name), ITEMS the number of order entries and TOTAL the gross final price in the order\(aqs currency (empty when Emporix sends only the deprecated totalPrice, which \fB\-o json\fR shows, as for an order that \fBepx orders add\-entries \-\-store\fR, \fBrecalculate\fR or \fBsplit\fR rewrote, and for sub\-orders). The orders of a legal entity: \fBepx orders list \-\-query legalEntityId:ID\fR.
.PP
Requires the order.order_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, STATUS, CREATED, CUSTOMER, SITE, ITEMS, TOTAL.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx orders patch"
Change members of an order.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders patch ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the members of the order ID that the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR gives, such as its shippingAddress or mixins, and keeps the others. Emporix does not check the order\(aqs metadata.version: it applies the change whatever version the body names, and does not answer a stale one with 409 Conflict; an unknown order is not found (exit 4). ID is the ID that \fBepx orders list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-completed\fR also requests the order.order_update_completed scope.
.PP
Requires the order.order_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-completed\fR
For an order that is COMPLETED, which Emporix changes only with one more scope (requests order.order_update_completed too).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-recalculate\fR
Have Emporix recalculate the whole order, coupon discounts included.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx orders recalculate"
Set the delivered amounts of an order and recalculate it.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders recalculate ORDER_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sets the amounts delivered of entries of the order ORDER_ID and recalculates the order: the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR holds entries, each with its entryId (an id in the order\(aqs entries, as \fBepx orders get ID \-o json\fR prints them) and deliveredAmount, and optionally deliveredAmountInPc and unit, the unit of deliveredAmount (e.g. GRM). Emporix refuses to recalculate a COMPLETED order with 400 Bad Request (exit 1), whatever the scopes.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Emporix answers with a sentence of text, which epx prints as a JSON string.
.PP
Requires the order.order_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx orders search"
Search orders.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the sales orders, personal data included, that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every order). It reads and shows them as \fBepx orders list\fR does.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Requires the order.order_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, STATUS, CREATED, CUSTOMER, SITE, ITEMS, TOTAL.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx orders split"
Split an order into sub\-orders by vendor.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders split ORDER_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Splits the order ORDER_ID into sub\-orders, one per vendor of its entries, sending splitBy VENDOR_ID, the only criterion that Emporix offers, unless \fB\-\-file\fR gives the body. Emporix splits only an order with status CREATED that was not split before and has no discounts: it becomes the MASTER_ORDER of the SUB_ORDERs that the response names. An order whose entries name no vendor stays as it is (the response names no subOrders); an order split before, or a sub\-order, is refused with 400 Bad Request (exit 1).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the order.order_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx orders transition"
Move an order to another status.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders transition ORDER_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Moves the order ORDER_ID to the status that \fB\-\-status\fR names, one that \fBepx orders transitions ORDER_ID\fR lists: CONFIRMED or DECLINED from CREATED, COMPLETED or DECLINED from CONFIRMED, and none from COMPLETED or DECLINED. Emporix refuses another with 403 Forbidden (exit 1) and says why, and answers the order\(aqs own status as done, without an entry in its history. ORDER_ID is the ID that \fBepx orders list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the order.order_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-status <STATUS>\fR
The STATUS to move the order to: IN_CHECKOUT, CREATED, CONFIRMED, DECLINED, SHIPPED or COMPLETED (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx orders transitions"
List the statuses an order can move to next.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders transitions ORDER_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the statuses that an order can move to next. ORDER_ID is the ID that \fBepx orders list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
Requires the order.order_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among STATUS.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx orders update"
Replace an order.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx orders update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the order ID with the order in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object as \fBepx orders get ID \-o json\fR prints it. Emporix does not check the order\(aqs metadata.version: it applies the change whatever version the body names, and does not answer a stale one with 409 Conflict; an unknown order is not found (exit 4). ID is the ID that \fBepx orders list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-completed\fR also requests the order.order_update_completed scope.
.PP
Requires the order.order_update scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-completed\fR
For an order that is COMPLETED, which Emporix changes only with one more scope (requests order.order_update_completed too).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-recalculate\fR
Have Emporix recalculate the whole order, coupon discounts included.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBepx\fR(1) for the global options, the credentials epx reads and its exit codes; https://commerce-cloud-integrations.github.io/emporix-cli/commands/orders
